  "liner": {
   "body_md": "Mountain Goats performed at Webster Hall in New York, NY, on Sunday, November 9, 2008 [1]. This audience recording, uploaded by nyctaper, captures 24 songs over 111 minutes [1]. The setlist includes tracks such as \"Have to Explode,\" \"Heretic Pride,\" and \"The House That Dripped Blood\" [1]. Notably, \"New Britain\" and \"It's All Here In Brownsville\" are the earliest archived performances of these songs [1]. The band also played \"Game Shows Touch Our Lives,\" which was a bustout not heard in the previous 26 archived shows [1]. The main set concluded with \"The Best Ever Death Metal Band In Denton\" [1]. Four encores followed, featuring \"Houseguest,\" \"Going To Georgia,\" \"No Children,\" and \"Palmcoder Yajna\" [1]. The final encore included a cover of Ace of Base's \"The Sign\" [1]. This recording is the only available capture of the show and has a documented lineage [1]. A poster for the event is credited to Themes [3]. The show was the 132nd in the archive's collection for the band, following a performance at Music Hall of Williamsburg the day before [2].",
